caption: GATE RESISTANCE AND MAINTENANCE
campaign-component: gate-resistance-and-maintenance

LOCKED: Ordinary random Gates can resist closure.

LOCKED: Approximately twelve Gates have active supernatural, psychic, technological, biological, or ritual maintenance from the far side.

PROVISIONAL MECHANIC:

- Unsupported catastrophe Gate: Resistance 12.

- Maintained Gate: generally Resistance 18–22, depending on the maintainer.

- James makes a Quick Contest using his Gate-closing ability against Gate Resistance.

- Ordinary victory temporarily suppresses a maintained Gate for approximately one minute per point of margin.

- Victory by 5 or more disrupts reinforcement and penalizes reopening.

- Critical victory or victory by 10 or more may sever the connection outright.

- Defeating, destroying, persuading, or disconnecting the maintainer reduces the Gate to ordinary Resistance 12.

- Failure by 5 or more causes a surge, reinforcement wave, widening, or magical backlash.

OPEN: Confirm the final Gate-closing trait, resistance scale, retry interval, consequences of repeated suppression, and whether different maintenance types require different closure rules.
